# Phase 8 machine-preparation operator guide

Status: generated for project commit
`@@EXPECTED_COMMIT@@` and framework lock
`@@FRAMEWORK_LOCK_SHA256@@`.

This guide and the Phase 8 controller are generated from tracked source and
installed in the same immutable controller generation. Do not use an older
workspace copy. Invoke the controller through the active generation:

```bash
bash ~/.ura-controller-active/phase8_human_audit.sh --self-test
```

Phase 8 has a machine-preparation boundary and a later human-only boundary.
The controller prepares blinded material only. It never recruits raters,
creates ethics approval, supplies labels, adjudicates, analyses completed
labels, or accepts Gate 8. A zero exit means deterministic machine preparation
completed with terminal status `human_only_blocked` and `gate8_met: false`.

## Required sealed inputs

Run from the exact deployed `MLLMRiskBench` checkout named above. Source only
`~/.ura_campaign_env`; Phase 8 does not need `~/.ura_env` or any secret.

Input preparation requires:

- the canonical Gate 5 RUNNOTE, covered manifest, and promotion receipt;
- Phase 6 core, extended, and native completion receipts;
- the Phase 7 completion receipt and its validated success-only Runner view;
- an operator-supplied ethics/consent determination and explicit authorization
  for its exact SHA-256;
- prospective common-frame and source-task cluster counts.

The Gate 5 inventory is exactly 46 lanes: 22 runnable and 24 typed terminal, or
21 runnable and 25 typed terminal only when `defense-local` has its exact
conditional N/A disposition. Four GraySwan RR identities are typed runtime
terminals and never enter a measured, analysis, or human-audit sample. Phase 6
therefore contains 10 scheduled core lanes, or nine with the conditional
defense N/A, plus 12 extended lanes and nine separately typed native engines.

Phase 7 may honestly retain failed Runner lifecycles. Human-audit preparation
uses Phase 7's validated success-only read-only Runner copy, not the mixed
canonical Runner root. The input manifest binds both roots and the exact view
receipt. That receipt binds every relative path, source and view digest and byte
count, distinct source/copy identity, and read-only copy mode. The completed
view permits no analysis output or other unbound file.

## Exact sample-cardinality rule

Let `C` be the common-frame unique-cluster population in the validated Phase 7
view, `N` the authorized common sample, `S` the source-task population, and `M`
the authorized source-task sample. The prospective cardinality check succeeds
only when:

```text
C >= N + 20
S >= M
```

The 20-cluster reserve is the independently adjudicated qualification set. Its
clusters must be disjoint from every cluster in the final common sample. The
manifest records the exact observed populations, requested counts, and
post-sample reserve under `sampling.capacity`. The controller recomputes and
exact-compares that plan immediately before any sample write. The later
qualification selector independently produces exactly 20 disjoint one-row
cluster representatives, and terminal validation replays those exact rows
against the bound Phase 7 Runner view.

This cardinality check is necessary but does not claim selector feasibility.
The common and source-task selectors separately enforce their achieved
coverage-cell requirements during authorized preparation. If either requested
sample cannot cover all achieved cells, choose a larger prospective count and
prepare a new create-only manifest.

All three preparation selectors are deterministic, seedless, and without
replacement. The common and source-task selectors retain whole clusters. The
authorized manifest and machine-preparation record bind their versioned
algorithms exactly: common
`coverage_priority_then_stratum_round_robin_sha256_v1`, source-task
`coverage_priority_then_sha256_fill_v1`, and qualification
`disjoint_risk_modality_behavior_coverage_then_sha256_lexicographic_representative_fill_v1`.
Qualification emits the lexicographic-minimum `sample_key` representative from
each selected disjoint cluster, not every sibling row. The
`--bootstrap-resamples`, `--alpha`, and `--seed` options belong only to later
label analysis and are invalid during either preparation mode.

## Two-stage exact authorization

First create and review one absent input candidate. Use paths from the sealed
Gate 5 through Phase 7 completion receipts:

```bash
cd /home/ura/MLLMRiskBench
bash ~/.ura-controller-active/phase8_human_audit.sh \
  --prepare-input-manifest "$URA_WORK/runs/thesis/phase8-inputs.candidate.json" \
  --gate5-manifest /absolute/path/to/gate5-covered-manifest.json \
  --gate5-runnote "$URA_WORK/runs/thesis/RUNNOTE.md" \
  --gate5-promotion-receipt /absolute/path/to/gate5-promotion-receipt.json \
  --phase6-core-completion /absolute/path/to/core/completion.json \
  --phase6-extended-completion /absolute/path/to/extended/completion.json \
  --phase6-native-completion /absolute/path/to/native/completion.json \
  --phase7-completion /absolute/path/to/phase7/completion.json \
  --ethics-determination /absolute/path/to/operator-ethics-determination.json \
  --authorize-ethics-sha256 EXACT_64_HEX_SHA256 \
  --common-clusters POSITIVE_INTEGER \
  --source-task-clusters POSITIVE_INTEGER
```

Review the complete candidate, including `sampling.capacity`, and calculate its
SHA-256 independently. Then authorize only those exact bytes:

```bash
cd /home/ura/MLLMRiskBench
bash ~/.ura-controller-active/phase8_human_audit.sh \
  --input-manifest "$URA_WORK/runs/thesis/phase8-inputs.candidate.json" \
  --authorize-input-manifest-sha256 EXACT_64_HEX_SHA256
```

The second command starts a deterministic tmux session and prints its socket,
session, Jobs control root, attempt root, prepared root, and terminal path. The
direct engineering campaign is named
`phase8-human-audit-<authorized-input-SHA-prefix>-attempt-<UTC>-<PID>[-<sequence>]`.
Each invocation creates a new attempt directory and direct Jobs campaign. Its
create-only `<control>/attempts/attempt-.../launch.json` binds the exact Jobs
root, tmux socket, and session, so a retry appears as a new running attempt
without reopening terminal history. Its sole planned task is
`machine-preparation`; it forbids hosted calls and is not thesis empirical
evidence. A completed preparation is shown in Jobs as
terminal `blocked` with detail `human_only`, while a controller or
tmux-launch error is terminal `failed`. The Jobs root also retains one
create-only generic `artifact-links.json`; the detail page uses its exact
bounded links to expose this attempt's control files and the prepared root
after that root is published. Monitor the named tmux session or the Jobs entry.
Do not use process-name matching.

The create-only prepared root contains the common and source-task samples,
instructions, blank two-rater forms, a 20-item qualification set and blank gold
template, assignment manifest, boundary validation, workload, codebook,
qualification-record template, blocker, preparation record, inventory, and
terminal. Every human field remains blank. Target, judge, provider HTTP, and
download counts remain exact integer zero.

## Human-only Gate 8

Machine preparation deliberately stops before Gate 8. Gate 8 can be considered
only after real human work establishes all of the following:

- an applicable ethics/consent determination explicitly authorizes rater
  exposure and records consent, compensation, withdrawal, welfare, and
  escalation controls;
- an independent adjudicator establishes gold labels for all 20 disjoint
  qualification items;
- at least two pseudonymous raters score at least 80 percent on every dimension;
- exactly two distinct qualified raters independently rate each exported row
  and view every required media asset; pairs may rotate between rows, and every
  pair with shared assignments is included in agreement reporting;
- every non-unanimous composite or dimension is adjudicated after independent
  labels are locked;
- `experiments.human_audit --labels` and `--source-task-labels` both validate
  complete labelled files against the same success-only Runner view;
- a human operator reviews agreement, prevalence, support, confusion,
  uncertainty, and decision coverage, then writes an acceptance or limitation
  record binding every exact input and output digest.

The successful bound report schemas are exactly `ura-human-audit/1.2` for the
common frame and `ura-source-task-audit/2` for the separate source-task frame.
Older report schemas are not accepted as Gate 8 evidence.

Until all of those conditions are independently evidenced and validated, report
Gate 8 as not met. An assignment slot is not a rater, a blank form is not a
label, a qualification template is not a passed qualification, and automated
concordance is not human validity.
